<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Kiziba</h1><p class="st-meta">1600 CE – 1963 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The northernmost Haya kingdom west of Lake Victoria, ruled by a Bito dynasty linked to Bunyoro.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Kiziba lay on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kagera-river">Kagera river</a> at the northern edge of today's <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/tanzania">Tanzania</a>. Its rulers belonged to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babiito-dynasty">Babito</a> clan, which traditions link with the royal house of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bunyoro">Kingdom of Bunyoro</a>, and it emerged as a separate kingdom by the 17th century.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The mukama governed a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haya-people">Haya</a> farming society growing bananas and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coffee-economy">coffee</a>, which was chewed as a stimulant and used in rituals. Kiziba kept its independence among rival Haya states and had close contacts with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-buganda">Buganda</a> to the north. Its court and royal rituals resembled those of other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-lakes">Great Lakes</a> kingdoms.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Kiziba became a subordinate chiefdom under <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/german-east-africa">German East Africa</a> and then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tanganyika-territory">British Tanganyika Territory</a>, ruled through its kings as a native authority. It ceased to exist when <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tanganyika">Tanganyika</a> abolished the chieftaincies in 1963.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1600 CE – 1963 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Horn and East Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:91.54%;width:7.22%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1600 CE – 1963 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Traditional religion, later Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Haya</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/tanzania">Tanzania</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kiziba</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1782&amp;focus=kingdom-of-kiziba" aria-label="Kingdom of Kiziba on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5654 2411 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Kiziba lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6087 2688h0M6087 2688h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5974 2667h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5974 2667h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Tanzania. <a href="/atlas?year=1782&amp;focus=kingdom-of-kiziba">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

